So normally Laravel does this for you, I think, but we handle things slightly differently (not using the `register()` method in the Exception Handler) since we don't always want errors like 429s sent to Rollbar. This PR adds those headers manually.

The error response now looks like this:

```
{
    "status": "error",
    "messages": "Too many requests. Try again in 40 seconds",
    "payload": {
        "requests_per_minute": 3,
        "retry-after": 40
    }
}
```

